> I am sorry, how again is this controversial? I haven't seen any comment indicating such.

@cart disagreed with this change last time it was attempted. (https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/pull/3893#issuecomment-1055247308) No one has picked up dynamic plugins and tried to improve it since deprecating it was last attempted.

Furthermore, I think `bevy_dynamic_plugin` even _existing_ in the main Bevy project is encouraging users to use it instead of making their own, better alternatives. As someone mentioned on Discord, Bevy has a reputation for reliability (partially due to being written in Rust). I would argue that dynamic plugins are quite _unreliable_, hurting this reputation. They are simple enough that if someone wanted to use them, they could just copy the code. I think they should do this, because it puts the responsibility on _them_ and not _us_.
